goroutine,lightweight thread of execution,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/goroutine.wav,go myFunction(),A function or method that runs concurrently with other functions or methods. They are managed by the Go runtime.
channel,typed conduit for communication,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/channel.wav,ch := make(chan int),A mechanism through which goroutines can communicate. They provide synchronization and prevent race conditions.
defer,postpones function execution,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/defer.wav,defer file.Close(),Schedules a function call to be run immediately before the function executing the defer returns.
package,Go's way of organizing code,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/package.wav,package main,A collection of source files in the same directory that are compiled together.
struct,composite data type,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/struct.wav,type Vertex struct { X, Y int },A collection of fields, useful for grouping data together to form records.
make,built-in function to create slices,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/make.wav,s := make([]int, 5),A built-in function that allocates and initializes an object of type slice, map, or chan only.
GOPATH,environment variable for Go projects,SourceImages/Sounds/Go/GOPATH.wav,Defines the root of your workspace,An environment variable that specifies the location of your Go workspace, where source code and binaries are stored.Promise,asynchronous operation object,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/Promise.wav,new Promise((resolve, reject) => ...),Represents the eventual completion (or failure) of an asynchronous operation and its resulting value.
async/await,syntactic sugar for Promises,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/AsyncAwait.wav,async function fetchData() { await fetch(...); },Keywords that allow writing asynchronous Promise-based code as if it were synchronous.
Closure,function with remembered scope,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/Closure.wav,"function outer() { let a=1; return () => a++; }",An inner function has access to the variables of its outer (enclosing) function, even after the outer function has returned.
Destructuring,unpacking values from data structures,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/Destructuring.wav,const { name, age } = user;,A syntax that makes it possible to unpack values from arrays or properties from objects into distinct variables.
Prototype,object inheritance mechanism,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/Prototype.wav,MyObject.prototype.myMethod = function() {},Mechanism by which JavaScript objects inherit features from one another.
Strict Equality,type and value comparison,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/StrictEquality.wav,if (a === b),The === operator checks for equality without performing type conversion; it is the preferred comparison operator.
Arrow Function,compact alternative to a function expression,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/ArrowFunction.wav,const add = (a, b) => a + b;,A shorter syntax for writing function expressions; does not have its own 'this' or 'arguments'.
Hoisting,default behavior of moving declarations,SourceImages/Sounds/JavaScript/Hoisting.wav,x = 5; var x;,JavaScript's default behavior of moving all declarations to the top of the current scope before code execution.JVM,Java Virtual Machine,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/JVM.wav,java -jar myapp.jar,An abstract machine that enables a computer to run a Java program. It provides the "write once, run anywhere" capability.
Garbage Collection,automatic memory management,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/GarbageCollection.wav,System.gc();,The process of finding and deleting objects that are no longer referenced by any part of the program, freeing up memory.
public static void main,main method entry point,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/psvm.wav,public static void main(String[] args),The standard method signature where program execution begins for a standalone Java application.
Interface,abstract type for behavior,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/Interface.wav,public interface Drivable { void drive(); },A reference type that can contain only constants, method signatures, default methods, and static methods.
final,non-changeable entity keyword,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/final.wav,final int MAX_USERS = 100;,A keyword used to mark a variable as unchangeable, a method as non-overridable, or a class as non-inheritable.
extends,class inheritance keyword,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/extends.wav,class Car extends Vehicle,Used to create a subclass that inherits the fields and methods of a superclass.
implements,interface implementation keyword,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/implements.wav,class Car implements Drivable,Used to indicate that a class is using the methods defined by an interface.
JAR,Java Archive,SourceImages/Sounds/Java/JAR.wav,A .jar file,A package file format used to aggregate many Java class files, associated metadata, and resources into one file.val/var,declaring variables,SourceImages/Sounds/Kotlin/valvar.wav,val a = 1; var b = 2;,`val` declares an immutable (read-only) variable, while `var` declares a mutable variable.
Null Safety,eliminates null pointer exceptions,SourceImages/Sounds/Kotlin/NullSafety.wav,var a: String? = "abc",The type system distinguishes between references that can hold null (nullable) and those that cannot (non-null).
data class,concise class for holding data,SourceImages/Sounds/Kotlin/DataClass.wav,data class User(val name: String),A class that is primarily used to hold data. The compiler automatically generates boilerplate like equals(), hashCode(), and toString().
Extension Function,adds functions to existing classes,SourceImages/Sounds/Kotlin/ExtensionFunction.wav,fun String.addExclamation(): String { return this + "!" },A mechanism to "add" new functions to any existing class without having to inherit from the class.
Coroutine,lightweight concurrency design pattern,SourceImages/Sounds/Kotlin/Coroutine.wav,GlobalScope.launch { ... },A way to write asynchronous, non-blocking code that is as easy to read as synchronous code.
when,advanced switch expression,SourceImages/Sounds/Kotlin/when.wav,when (x) { 1 -> print("one"), else -> ... },An expression that can be used as a more powerful and flexible replacement for the traditional switch statement.word,translation,soundFile,exampleSentence,exampleSentenceTranslation
aqua,water,SourceImages/Sounds/Latin/Aqua.wav,Aqua vitae fons est.,Water is the fountain of life.
